<title>POLAND: Espebepe extends Wednesday's tumble.</title>
<headline>Espebepe extends Wednesday's tumble.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish debt-ridden builder Espebepe SA, down 9.6 percent on Thursday to 4.7 zlotys, extended Wednesday's plunge as speculators continued to play on the firm's unclear fate, traders said.</p>
<p>The firm had surged 41.9 percent last week after the previous week's steep fall.</p>
<p>Last month Espebepe, which has 75 million zlotys in debts and faces the risk of bankruptcy, had a creditors' meeting postponed to April 14.</p>
<p>Selling was strong enough after price-fixing for investors to have their bids reduced.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
